{"name":"Breathe","hex":"#d1d2b8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breathe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw air into (inhale), and expel air from (exhale), the lungs in order to extract oxygen and excrete waste gases.","To take in needed gases and expel waste gases in a similar way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breathe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breathing","blocks":[{"text":"Breathing is the rhythmic process of inhaling air into the lungs providing oxygen, and exhaling the air removing carbon dioxide, in the gas exchange process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Real-time_MRI_-_Thorax.ogv/330px--Real-time_MRI_-_Thorax.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathing","wikidata":"Q9530"},{"title":"Breathe (2017 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Breathe is a 2017 biographical drama film directed by Andy Serkis in his directorial debut, from a screenplay by William Nicholson. It is based on the true story of Robin Cavendish, who became paralysed from the neck down by polio at the age of 28. The film stars Andrew Garfield, Claire Foy, Hugh Bonneville, Tom Hollander, Ed Speleers and Dean-Charles Chapman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/BreathePoster2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathe_(2017_film)","wikidata":"Q27703270"},{"title":"Breathe (British band)","blocks":[{"text":"Breathe were an English pop band formed in London in 1984. The band enjoyed chart success in the late 1980s and early 1990s with hit singles \"Don't Tell Me Lies\", \"How Can I Fall?\" and \"Say a Prayer\". The group's biggest hit was \"Hands to Heaven\", which reached No. 2 in the United States in August 1988."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/73/Breathe_band_photo.jpg/330px-Breathe_band_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathe_(British_band)","wikidata":"Q2307431"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg/500px-Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg/1280px-Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg/500px-Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibcage_during_inhalation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Costillas_%28gray%29.png/330px-Costillas_%28gray%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Costillas_%28gray%29.png/330px-Costillas_%28gray%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACostillas_(gray).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Quiet_breathing.jpg/500px-Quiet_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Quiet_breathing.jpg/1280px-Quiet_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Quiet_breathing.jpg/500px-Quiet_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuiet_breathing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Forceful_breathing.jpg/500px-Forceful_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Forceful_breathing.jpg/1280px-Forceful_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Forceful_breathing.jpg/500px-Forceful_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForceful_breathing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Nose_in_cold_weather.gif/500px-Nose_in_cold_weather.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Nose_in_cold_weather.gif/1280px-Nose_in_cold_weather.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Nose_in_cold_weather.gif/500px-Nose_in_cold_weather.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inhaled air is warmed and moistened by the wet, warm nasal mucosa, which consequently cools and dries. When warm, wet air from the lungs is breathed out through the nose, the cold hygroscopic mucus in the cool and dry nose re-captures some of the warmth and moisture from that exhaled air. In very cold weather the re-captured water may cause a \"dripping nose\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANose_in_cold_weather.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg/250px-Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg/250px-Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The lower airways:TracheaMainstem bronchusLobar bronchusSegmental bronchusBronchioleAlveolar ductAlveolus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllu_quiz_lung05.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_%28Santana_Tribute%29_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_%288%29.JPG/500px-Bak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_%28Santana_Tribute%29_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_%288%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_%28Santana_Tribute%29_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_%288%29.JPG/1280px-Bak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_%28Santana_Tribute%29_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_%288%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_%28Santana_Tribute%29_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_%288%29.JPG/500px-Bak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_%28Santana_Tribute%29_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_%288%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Following on from the above diagram, if the exhaled air is breathed out through the mouth in cold and humid conditions, the water vapor will condense into a visible cloud or mist.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABak%C3%B3_%C3%81rp%C3%A1d_-_Milagro_(Santana_Tribute)_egy%C3%BCttes%2C_Miskolc%2C_2015.02.07_(8).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Altitude_and_air_pressure_%26_Everest.jpg/500px-Altitude_and_air_pressure_%26_Everest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Altitude_and_air_pressure_%26_Evere